    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (68.96) and **Christian Yelich** (68.23) leading the offensive charge. **Trea Turner** remains the cornerstone of our lineup, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Sandy Alcantara and a 10% boost for hitting at the top of the order. His BvP history (46 PA) provides an extra layer of confidence in his ability to manufacture the stolen bases we desperately need. Simultaneously, **Christian Yelich** is in a prime spot against Landen Roupp; the combination of a 13% platoon edge and favorable wind conditions makes him an elite play. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.24) and **Kyle Schwarber** (63.94) also cleared the 60-point threshold comfortably, the Zebras\u2019 focus is on maximizing high-on-base, high-speed profiles to capitalize on our scarce stolen base category.\n\nDepth management remains critical, as evidenced by our most difficult decision involving **Jacob Gonzalez**. With a score of 50.77, **Jacob Gonzalez** was the strongest candidate on the bench, trailing the utility spot occupied by **Lars Nootbaar** (58.67) by nearly eight points. While **Jacob Gonzalez** faced a mediocre arm in Brandon Pfaadt, the optimizer favored **Lars Nootbaar** due to a massive 11% boost from dynamic platoon splits against Colin Rea. We have opted to bench **Jacob Gonzalez** not only due to this efficiency gap but also because of a 31% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Dillon Dingler** and **Kazuma Okamoto**, as any shift downward in the batting order would force a re-evaluation of their projected daily efficiency scores.",
